UPCOMING EVENTS (1 MINUTE PER PERSON)  {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced that it is Earth Month and noted that the organization will be participating in several community events. He also provided tips on home organics recycling, including freezing food scraps before placing them in the organics bin to reduce odors on collection day and adding baking soda to help minimize smells.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Library Manager Cassandra Sargent thanked the Fire Department for hosting a successful story time event last week, noting that several attendees learned about fire safety. She announced an upcoming Writer\rquote s Workshop titled \ldblquote How to Start Writing Your Book,\rdblquote  scheduled for Tuesday, April 14, 2026, from 5:00 PM to 7:00 PM. She also announced the launch of a new speaker series, presented in collaboration with the City\rquote s Library Commission, featuring best-selling author Julia Quinn at the Mira Costa High School Auditorium on Saturday, May 23, 2026, at 2:00 PM.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Environmental Programs Administrator Britny Coker-Moen invited the community to the City\rquote s Earth Day Tree Planting event, held in partnership with Grades of Green, at Veteran\rquote s Parkway on Saturday, April 18, 2026, from 9:30 AM to 1:00 PM. She also announced a \ldblquote Bioblitz by the Dunes\rdblquote  event, in collaboration with the Bay Foundation and other organizations, at Rosecrans Avenue and The Strand on Saturday, April 25, 2026, from 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM. In addition, she shared that the City is offering a full month of activities for the community and that participants may pick up a stamp card at City Hall to track completed activities for a chance to earn a prize.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Mayor Lesser introduced the City\rquote s new Assistant City Clerk, Patricia Matson, noting that she has worked for the City for several years and welcomed her to the role. He also invited the community to attend his final \ldblquote Coffee with the Mayor\rdblquote  at Metlox Plaza on Friday, May 1, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf2\i0\f1\par
}


