7.. Consideration of a Resolution Authorizing the City Manager to Execute an Agreement with Circuit Transit Inc. for a Six-Month On-Demand Point-to-Point Local Microtransit Service Pilot Project and Appropriation of up to $540,626 in Proposition A Local Return Funds (Unbudgeted) (Community Development Department Director Alkire).
(Estimated Time: 1 Hr. and 30 Mins.)
A)	DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION
B)	ADOPT RESOLUTION NO. 26-0031
C)	APPROPRIATE FUNDS  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Nina Trieu Tarnay {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Community Development Director Masa Alkire provided background on the item and introduced Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet who provided the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line Traffic Engineer Zandvliet, Finance Director Libby Bretthauer, Circuit Transit Inc. Vice President of Business Development Daniel Kramer and Parks and Recreation Director Mark Leyman responded to City Council questions.\line\line Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual(s) spoke:\line\line Stefan Kampe\line Jim Burton\line Kelly Stroman\line Jill Lamkin\line Carol Patterson\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line\pard Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line Councilmember Tarnay made a motion to direct staff to proceed with a hybrid of Service Alternatives\u8239?1 and\u8239?2; to explore a reduced fare for seniors so the rate is lower than $5.00, with a regular fare for non-seniors; to adjust the service hours to 12:00\u8239?PM to 9:00\u8239?PM Monday through Thursday, 12:00\u8239?PM to 10:00\u8239?PM on Friday and Saturday, and 12:00\u8239?PM to 8:00\u8239?PM on Sunday; to evaluate the feasibility of charging vehicles at the Public Works Yard to offset costs; and to include advertising revenue opportunities.\line\line Councilmember Howorth inquired if Councilmember Tarnay would consider adjusting the start time to 11:00 AM, if needed during the pilot program, and postponing the use of vehicle advertisements while exploring corporate sponsorship opportunities that do not include alcohol.\line\line Councilmember Tarnay accepted the request.\cf1\i0\f1\par
}


