\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Councilmember Tarnay requested to agendize a discussion to explore code amendments that would align the North Manhattan Beach business parking requirements with those of the Downtown Manhattan Beach area. Councilmember Charelian concurred.\line\line Councilmember Charelian requested to agendize a discussion on ways to further educate public safety personnel and downtown businesses regarding interactions with First Amendment auditors. Councilmember Howorth concurred.\line\line Mayor Lesser also requested that the discussion include public education on what distinguishes lawful First Amendment activity from harassment.\line\line City Attorney Quinn Barrow responded to City Council questions and stated that staff will research and evaluate alternatives and will provide a confidential informational memo to the City Council once the research is complete.\line\line\pard Mayor Pro Tem Franklin requested to agendize a discussion to consider opposing Los Angeles County\rquote s June 2 ballot measure, the Essential Services Restoration Act, which would add a 0.5% increase to the Countywide general sales tax for homelessness services. Mayor Lesser concurred.\cf1\i0\f1\par
